WEBVTT

00:00:31.990 --> 00:00:34.576
So I gave the cookies
you made to Fawn and the kids,

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:36.703
and they couldn't believe it.

00:00:36.828 --> 00:00:40.040
They were delicious! But I digress.

00:00:40.123 --> 00:00:44.378
Tremble, puny earthlings!
One day, my race will destroy you all.

00:00:47.339 --> 00:00:49.091
Could one of you guys get that?

00:00:56.431 --> 00:00:58.684
It's a doorbell baby!

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:02.646
Hello, little guy. You know,
I was abandoned as a baby, too.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:05.023
- So...
- Garbage, huh? I'll take care of it.

00:01:05.148 --> 00:01:07.025
Bender, stop!

00:01:07.109 --> 00:01:09.319
- It's a baby!
- A baby what?

00:01:09.611 --> 00:01:10.612
Ow!

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:16.034
Oh, it's just a card!
From the orphanarium I grew up in.

00:01:17.661 --> 00:01:20.581
Leela, you're invited to a reunion

00:01:20.664 --> 00:01:24.209
at Cookieville Minimum-Security
Orphanarium.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:26.962
Please stand clear
of self-destructing basket.

00:01:28.839 --> 00:01:31.675
A reunion at your old orphanarium, eh?

00:01:31.758 --> 00:01:34.511
- You gonna go?
- No way, Josébot.

00:01:34.595 --> 00:01:36.763
I never want to see
those other orphans again.

00:01:36.847 --> 00:01:39.600
Not after the way they used to pick on me.

00:01:39.683 --> 00:01:42.394
One Eye, One Eye, One Eye!

00:01:42.477 --> 00:01:44.855
Nice depth perception, One Eye!

00:01:46.857 --> 00:01:49.735
How can you make fun of me, Kirk?
You're blind!

00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:53.113
My eyes may not work,
but at least I got two of them.

00:01:59.870 --> 00:02:01.788
Aw, that's terrible, Leela.

00:02:01.872 --> 00:02:04.833
But imagine the look on their faces
when you show up with two friends

00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:06.502
who eat all the hors d'oeuvres.

00:02:06.585 --> 00:02:10.339
Well, I wouldn't mind rubbing my success
in a few choice faces.

00:02:10.422 --> 00:02:12.341
Set a course for adventure!

00:02:19.097 --> 00:02:20.599
- Ew!
- What a dump!

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:23.393
Just like old times.

00:02:24.419 --> 00:02:28.965
Gosh, the bars on the windows seemed
so much thicker back then.

00:02:31.259 --> 00:02:33.136
Mr. Vogel? Remember me?

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:34.429
Leela!

00:02:34.513 --> 00:02:36.890
You're worthless,
and no one will ever love you!

00:02:38.100 --> 00:02:40.644
You used to say that all the time.

00:02:40.769 --> 00:02:42.813
Oh, those were happier days.

00:02:49.486 --> 00:02:50.487
Mmm!

00:02:50.612 --> 00:02:52.990
The "gristle in a blanket" isn't half bad.

00:02:53.949 --> 00:02:57.452
And try one of these Popsicle sticks.
They've absorbed quite a bit of flavor.

00:02:57.536 --> 00:03:00.706
Hey, look. It's our old group picture.

00:03:01.748 --> 00:03:04.167
I don't see you anywhere.

00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:06.336
That's me, over in Cootie-town.

00:03:07.129 --> 00:03:09.214
Get a load
of this average-looking guy.

00:03:09.297 --> 00:03:10.549
That's Adlai Atkins.

00:03:10.632 --> 00:03:12.634
I used to have kind of a crush on him.

00:03:14.177 --> 00:03:15.846
One Eye, One Eye!

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:21.727
- Stupid as a French guy!
- One Eye, One Eye, One Eye...

00:03:29.318 --> 00:03:32.237
Well, it's time to say
hello to the old gang.

00:03:41.038 --> 00:03:43.957
So? What you been up to
since you left the orphanarium?

00:03:44.082 --> 00:03:47.419
Oh, livin' in a box,
fightin' the shakes. You?

00:03:47.502 --> 00:03:50.172
Sellin' kidneys, teeth.
Whatever falls out of me.

00:03:50.255 --> 00:03:54.593
And what am I up to, you ask?
Why, I'm a very successful space captain.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:56.470
- Oh...
- Wow.

00:03:56.553 --> 00:03:58.013
How nice for you, Leela.

00:03:58.096 --> 00:04:01.266
That's so good for a person with one eye.

00:04:01.350 --> 00:04:04.519
Hey! You can't feel sorry for me.

00:04:04.544 --> 00:04:07.547
I'm a space captain,
and you're a bunch of losers.

00:04:07.731 --> 00:04:10.901
Right. Right. We're the losers.

00:04:12.277 --> 00:04:14.655
Well, if it isn't old One Eye?

00:04:16.698 --> 00:04:20.160
Oh, yeah? Well, shut up, Cane Boy!

00:04:20.243 --> 00:04:21.953
He can't hear you. He's deaf now.

00:04:22.037 --> 00:04:23.372
Leave Leela alone.

00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:25.666
She's leading a perfectly normal life.

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:29.336
She's not gussied up, duded out,
getting down, or where it's at.

00:04:29.516 --> 00:04:31.059
Now, run along.

00:04:33.382 --> 00:04:34.633
Thanks, Adlai.

00:04:34.716 --> 00:04:37.636
I guess you never really
outgrow being an eyeball...

00:04:37.719 --> 00:04:38.804
Oddball.

00:04:38.887 --> 00:04:43.016
Nonsense, you're a space captain.
That's a fine, conventional profession.

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:46.728
Well, you know.
It's just for a package delivery service.

00:04:46.812 --> 00:04:50.315
Ah, ah! A package is just
a box until it's delivered.

00:04:50.774 --> 00:04:52.693
Huh. I'd never thought of it that way.

00:04:52.776 --> 00:04:54.444
So what do you do these days?

00:04:54.528 --> 00:04:55.737
Oh, I'm a doctor.

00:04:55.821 --> 00:04:57.990
A tall doctor, you say.

00:05:05.038 --> 00:05:06.873
Sir? You seem pretty stable.

00:05:06.957 --> 00:05:08.750
Have you thought about adopting a kid?

00:05:08.834 --> 00:05:09.835
Sure haven't.

00:05:09.918 --> 00:05:11.378
Well, keep adoption in mind.

00:05:11.461 --> 00:05:13.505
It's a great way to have a kid
without having sex.

00:05:13.588 --> 00:05:15.007
Really?

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:19.302
Plus, the government will help out
with a small stipend of $100 a week.

00:05:19.386 --> 00:05:21.096
$100 a week?

00:05:24.933 --> 00:05:27.185
I'm so sorry I teased you back then.

00:05:27.269 --> 00:05:28.478
Let me make it up to you.

00:05:28.562 --> 00:05:30.939
I can fix it so no one
ever makes fun of you again.

00:05:31.023 --> 00:05:32.607
You mean, by beating them up?

00:05:32.691 --> 00:05:35.193
Because I've broken that blind kid's nose,
like, 10 times,

00:05:35.277 --> 00:05:36.653
and it doesn't make a difference.

00:05:36.737 --> 00:05:39.740
No, I specialize in phaser eye surgery.

00:05:39.823 --> 00:05:43.618
I can build you a paraffin eye
and graft it on with skin from your foot.

00:05:43.702 --> 00:05:48.290
It won't be able to see, but you'll look
like a perfectly normal, two-eyed person.

00:05:49.041 --> 00:05:51.918
Me? Perfectly normal?

00:05:54.379 --> 00:05:55.756
Mmm...

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.462
Sons, daughters, meet Uncle Fry.

00:06:02.546 --> 00:06:05.632
Hey, why are those kids following you?
Do you have candy stuck to your ass?

00:06:05.716 --> 00:06:08.510
No, it's called "parenting."

00:06:08.593 --> 00:06:09.928
Come on, dumplings.

00:06:10.012 --> 00:06:12.597
We've got 12 government stipends
to collect.

00:06:12.681 --> 00:06:15.475
- Yeah!
- Our daddy's a giant toy!

00:06:16.977 --> 00:06:19.688
Phaser eye surgery
is a capital idea.

00:06:19.771 --> 00:06:24.234
I'm sure Leela's tired of morons
gaping at her eye all the time.

00:06:25.652 --> 00:06:26.903
Oh...

00:06:27.362 --> 00:06:29.906
I think cosmetic surgery's great, Leela.

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:33.452
I used to be too cute,
so I had cuteness reduction surgery,

00:06:33.535 --> 00:06:35.495
here and here.

00:06:35.579 --> 00:06:38.332
You guys are crazy.
Leela doesn't need surgery.

00:06:38.415 --> 00:06:40.042
You look great the way you are.

00:06:40.292 --> 00:06:42.878
Oh, that's so sweet, Fry.

00:06:42.961 --> 00:06:45.547
But for once in my life,
I just want to look normal.

00:06:45.631 --> 00:06:48.050
But you're better than normal.
You're abnormal.

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:50.636
If you ask me, you shouldn't
care what other people think.

00:06:50.719 --> 00:06:53.930
You're right!
I'll start by not caring what you think.

00:06:54.014 --> 00:06:55.682
I'm getting the surgery!

00:06:55.766 --> 00:06:57.142
- That-a-girl!
- Right on!

00:06:57.225 --> 00:06:58.894
- Good call.
- Wonderful.

00:06:58.977 --> 00:07:00.354
And while you're under the knife,

00:07:00.437 --> 00:07:03.607
you could also get an ink pouch
to help you escape your enemies.

00:07:03.690 --> 00:07:06.735
That's the stupidest idea I've ever heard,
you imbecile.

00:07:15.160 --> 00:07:17.746
Now, we'll find out
if the operation was a success.

00:07:18.239 --> 00:07:19.741
Hold onto your hats.

00:07:30.884 --> 00:07:32.970
Oh, I'm sorry. This is the wrong patient.

00:07:54.324 --> 00:07:55.367
Whoops!

00:08:04.251 --> 00:08:06.837
Leela, those eyes look so great on you.

00:08:07.087 --> 00:08:09.131
Bah! I think she looked fine before.

00:08:09.214 --> 00:08:10.757
- No!
- Wrong.

00:08:10.924 --> 00:08:12.634
Wow! Look at me!

00:08:13.468 --> 00:08:15.846
Although I don't have
the hang of blinking yet.

00:08:15.929 --> 00:08:16.930
You'll get it.

00:08:17.014 --> 00:08:20.183
Personally, I try not to blink too much
because it seems flashy.

00:08:20.267 --> 00:08:22.185
But when I do, I enjoy it.

00:08:23.562 --> 00:08:25.939
I did it! I blunk!

00:08:26.023 --> 00:08:28.859
And just in time
to screw up this picture I took.

00:08:28.942 --> 00:08:30.110
Hooray!

00:08:44.416 --> 00:08:47.919
Pretty woman
Walkin' down the street

00:08:48.003 --> 00:08:49.129
Pretty woman

00:08:49.212 --> 00:08:50.213
Ow, ow, ow...

00:08:50.297 --> 00:08:54.384
The kind I like to meet
Pretty woman

00:08:54.468 --> 00:08:58.138
I don't believe you
You're not the truth

00:08:58.221 --> 00:09:02.017
No one could look as good as you

00:09:04.770 --> 00:09:06.480
Mercy

00:09:11.526 --> 00:09:12.778
Pretty woman

00:09:12.861 --> 00:09:15.197
I've never felt so unremarkable!

00:09:15.280 --> 00:09:18.116
Today, I actually blended in with a crowd!

00:09:25.207 --> 00:09:27.834
Kids, meet the jerkbags I work with.

00:09:27.918 --> 00:09:29.878
Hello, jerkbags!

00:09:29.962 --> 00:09:33.006
Oh, they're so cute! What are their names?

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:34.257
Kids have names?

00:09:34.341 --> 00:09:37.302
My name is Nina, and his name's Albert...

00:09:37.386 --> 00:09:39.680
And from now on,
you're all named Bender, Jr!

00:09:40.681 --> 00:09:43.517
Looky here.
My first government stipend check.

00:09:43.600 --> 00:09:47.020
Twelve baby humans, 1,200 wing-wangs.

00:09:48.313 --> 00:09:51.733
Daddy Bender, we're hungry.

00:09:51.817 --> 00:09:56.238
What is it with you kids?
Every other day, it's food, food, food!

00:09:58.240 --> 00:10:01.576
Oh, fine. I'll get you some stupid food.

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:03.412
Could we have Bender Burgers again?

00:10:03.495 --> 00:10:05.497
No! The cat shelter's on to me.

00:10:09.459 --> 00:10:10.585
Hello, Leela.

00:10:10.669 --> 00:10:13.964
I was at a nearby tailor, getting one
of my Hawaiian shirts toned down,

00:10:14.047 --> 00:10:16.133
so I thought I'd drop in
for your follow-up exam.

00:10:16.425 --> 00:10:18.593
Oh! That's so handsome of you.

00:10:18.677 --> 00:10:20.887
Just follow the light with your eyes.

00:10:23.307 --> 00:10:24.308
Perfect.

00:10:24.391 --> 00:10:27.477
You know, a guy could fall
head over heels for a gal like you.

00:10:27.561 --> 00:10:29.646
As for me, I'm somewhat interested myself.

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.939
What are you saying?

00:10:31.023 --> 00:10:32.691
I've never been good with words,

00:10:32.774 --> 00:10:35.402
which is why I'm in
such a delicate conundrum.

00:10:35.485 --> 00:10:37.654
- Will you go out with me this Sunday?
- Sure!

00:10:38.864 --> 00:10:41.325
I don't know what else to say,
so I'll just say it.

00:10:41.408 --> 00:10:43.285
Okeydokey, see you then.

00:10:44.244 --> 00:10:47.998
This is so unfair. I liked you back
when you were a Cyclops.

00:10:48.081 --> 00:10:50.334
That guy's only interested
now that you have two eyes.

00:10:50.417 --> 00:10:51.793
You're just jealous.

00:10:51.877 --> 00:10:53.003
No, I'm not!

00:10:53.086 --> 00:10:56.131
Oh, wait, I am!
But my point remains valid.

00:10:56.214 --> 00:10:59.051
Fry, I just want to try
dating a normal man,

00:10:59.134 --> 00:11:02.095
who, if you go somewhere with him,
no one says he's crummy.

00:11:02.179 --> 00:11:04.681
I think I deserve that once in life.

00:11:04.765 --> 00:11:06.725
Be careful with that Adlai, Leela.

00:11:06.808 --> 00:11:08.852
He's a doctor. They're very poor.

00:11:08.936 --> 00:11:10.938
Actually, most doctors are rich.

00:11:11.021 --> 00:11:13.649
What? When did this happen?
You're joking, right?

00:11:13.732 --> 00:11:15.275
That's not funny!

00:11:17.986 --> 00:11:20.113
Okay, they got everything you need here.

00:11:20.197 --> 00:11:21.782
Booze, a couple of peanuts...

00:11:21.865 --> 00:11:23.492
They got a crapper in the back.

00:11:23.575 --> 00:11:25.744
That's one of the things
you kids do, right?

00:11:25.827 --> 00:11:27.537
- Yeah!
- Then knock yourself out.

00:11:29.247 --> 00:11:30.415
Hey! Hey!

00:11:30.499 --> 00:11:33.669
Only eat and drink enough
to barely keep yourselves alive.

00:11:33.752 --> 00:11:35.796
I'm tryin' to make a profit here.

00:11:39.716 --> 00:11:42.636
Daddy, Bethany's hitting me!

00:11:42.719 --> 00:11:43.845
Here.

00:11:46.848 --> 00:11:48.183
These kids yours?

00:11:48.266 --> 00:11:49.685
- Yeah.
- Ooh.

00:11:49.768 --> 00:11:52.688
I'm attracted to
a man with responsibility.

00:11:52.771 --> 00:11:55.857
That's me, baby.
Let me just ditch the kids in an alley,

00:11:55.941 --> 00:11:58.527
and we can go have some fun.

00:11:58.735 --> 00:12:00.696
- Daddy Bender?
- Son?

00:12:00.779 --> 00:12:03.907
Daddy's tryin' to score
with a cheap floozy right now,

00:12:03.991 --> 00:12:06.785
so he needs you to cram a Tinkertoy in it.

00:12:06.868 --> 00:12:09.663
I love you, Daddy Bender.

00:12:09.746 --> 00:12:11.498
Hey! What the hell are you doin'?

00:12:11.581 --> 00:12:14.126
- Quit huggin' me.
- I guess you're busy.

00:12:14.209 --> 00:12:15.544
I'll catch you later.

00:12:15.627 --> 00:12:18.213
You morons!
I don't know what you're tryin' to pull,

00:12:18.297 --> 00:12:20.882
but I got half a mind to hug each
and every one of you

00:12:20.966 --> 00:12:22.217
and see how you like it!

00:12:22.301 --> 00:12:23.635
- Yeah!
- Argh...

00:12:24.553 --> 00:12:25.679
Come on.

00:12:26.054 --> 00:12:27.055
Argh!

00:12:30.017 --> 00:12:32.102
I thought I'd take you someplace ordinary.

00:12:32.185 --> 00:12:35.397
- A place no one could object to.
- That sounds wonderful.

00:12:42.362 --> 00:12:45.907
I'd like an extra-beautiful bouquet,
for my extra-gorgeous sweetheart.

00:12:49.703 --> 00:12:51.246
Average, please.

00:12:53.915 --> 00:12:57.044
Oh, Adlai,
I've had a wonderful time today.

00:12:57.127 --> 00:13:00.339
No one's stared at me,
or avoided staring at me,

00:13:00.422 --> 00:13:02.174
or tried to burn me.

00:13:02.257 --> 00:13:04.801
You make me feel so not weird.

00:13:04.885 --> 00:13:09.431
Leela, you're 999,999 in a million.

00:13:23.445 --> 00:13:25.697
Thanks for comin' out
to get to know my boyfriend.

00:13:25.781 --> 00:13:27.115
Isn't he dreamy?

00:13:27.199 --> 00:13:28.575
Totally.

00:13:31.787 --> 00:13:36.249
Listen. I just want you all to know,
your Leela's one standard lady.

00:13:36.333 --> 00:13:38.585
Oh, Adlai! Stop.

00:13:38.669 --> 00:13:41.213
What's so wonderful
about Leela being normal?

00:13:41.296 --> 00:13:44.257
The rest of us aren't normal,
and that's what makes us great.

00:13:44.383 --> 00:13:45.926
Like Dr. Zoidberg.

00:13:46.009 --> 00:13:49.137
He's a weird monster who smells
like he eats garbage, and does.

00:13:49.221 --> 00:13:50.222
Damn right!

00:13:50.305 --> 00:13:53.183
And the professor's
a senile, amoral crackpot.

00:13:54.685 --> 00:13:56.895
Hermes is a Rastafarian accountant.

00:13:56.979 --> 00:13:58.188
Tally me banana!

00:13:58.272 --> 00:14:00.107
Amy's a klutz from Mars.

00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.191
Oops!

00:14:01.275 --> 00:14:03.652
And, Fry, you've got that brain thing!

00:14:03.735 --> 00:14:06.822
I already did.
So, Leela, do you want to be like us?

00:14:06.905 --> 00:14:08.532
Or do you want to be like Adlai,

00:14:08.615 --> 00:14:12.244
with no severe mental or social
problems whatsoever?

00:14:13.078 --> 00:14:15.497
That's the dumbest question I ever heard.

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:16.873
- She's right!
- No doubt!

00:14:16.957 --> 00:14:17.958
- Duh!
- Daylight come.

00:14:18.458 --> 00:14:20.294
Comin' through. Watch your head.

00:14:21.211 --> 00:14:22.629
Help! I'm under attack!

00:14:24.923 --> 00:14:26.842
Remember your manners, kids.

00:14:26.925 --> 00:14:29.720
Forks go in the left pocket,
spoons in the right.

00:14:29.803 --> 00:14:34.057
Which one of you cutie muffins
gets the children's spicy squab?

00:14:34.141 --> 00:14:35.350
Me!

00:14:35.475 --> 00:14:38.729
What do we say
when someone gives you something?

00:14:38.812 --> 00:14:41.231
- 'Bout time!
- That's my boy!

00:14:42.107 --> 00:14:44.192
And here's your check. Bam!

00:14:46.111 --> 00:14:47.529
I gotta go poopy.

00:14:47.613 --> 00:14:50.532
You should've gone poopy before
it was time to run out on the check!

00:14:50.616 --> 00:14:52.451
Come on! Go! Go! Through the kitchen!

00:14:52.534 --> 00:14:55.370
You little crooks! If I catch you,

00:14:55.454 --> 00:14:57.914
I'm gonna make cutie muffin gumbo!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.042
You know,

00:15:00.125 --> 00:15:03.211
seeing that strange robot
force 12 children to do his bidding

00:15:03.295 --> 00:15:04.838
makes me think about kids of our own.

00:15:04.921 --> 00:15:08.425
Us? Me? You? Kids?

00:15:08.508 --> 00:15:12.054
That's correct. It's time
to stop living this vida bachelor loca.

00:15:12.137 --> 00:15:13.513
Settle down and have kids.

00:15:13.597 --> 00:15:15.015
Oh, Adlai.

00:15:15.098 --> 00:15:18.101
This is the most beautiful
moment of my life.

00:15:28.236 --> 00:15:30.447
Daddy Bender, I want a piggyback ride!

00:15:30.530 --> 00:15:33.659
Daddy's tired.
Let's just have another dog pile on Fry.

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:36.328
Oh!

00:15:38.872 --> 00:15:40.999
Tell us a story, Daddy Bender.

00:15:41.083 --> 00:15:43.835
Story, story, story!

00:15:43.919 --> 00:15:45.879
All right, fine. Gather around.

00:15:46.004 --> 00:15:47.714
Yeah!

00:15:48.507 --> 00:15:50.842
We wanna hear this one again.

00:15:53.387 --> 00:15:55.430
"Bender's Arrest Record.

00:15:55.514 --> 00:15:57.265
"By the Police.

00:15:57.349 --> 00:15:59.643
"On March 3, at 2:00 p.m.,

00:15:59.726 --> 00:16:01.687
"Bender was caught shoplifting."

00:16:01.770 --> 00:16:03.522
Yeah. Show us the picture.

00:16:06.441 --> 00:16:07.526
There he is.

00:16:07.609 --> 00:16:10.487
Okay, kids. It's 9:00,
and you know what that means.

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:13.240
Daddy's sick of lookin' at ya,
so go to bed.

00:16:13.949 --> 00:16:15.033
Aw!

00:16:15.242 --> 00:16:17.828
The grown-ups have to talk. Come on, Ma.

00:16:22.499 --> 00:16:25.711
Now, to figure out how much money
I'm rakin' in off those twerps.

00:16:32.175 --> 00:16:34.136
Oh! I need a calculator.

00:16:34.219 --> 00:16:35.470
You are a calculator.

00:16:35.554 --> 00:16:37.806
I mean, a good calculator.

00:16:37.889 --> 00:16:40.892
Minus the food,
the bunny rabbit wallpaper...

00:16:41.184 --> 00:16:45.063
I'm gettin' 100 bucks a kid,
and they're costin' me 110!

00:16:45.314 --> 00:16:47.566
There goes
my new kitchen cabinets.

00:16:47.649 --> 00:16:50.152
I'm not sittin' through
one more PTA meeting!

00:16:50.235 --> 00:16:52.112
The kids have got to go.

00:16:52.571 --> 00:16:55.198
Daddy, how do I flush you?

00:16:55.282 --> 00:16:56.908
Just go to bed!

00:17:09.880 --> 00:17:13.258
You know, doing this jigsaw puzzle
of a pacifier factory

00:17:13.342 --> 00:17:15.969
makes me want to have children
with you all the more.

00:17:16.053 --> 00:17:17.971
Adlai, I was thinking.

00:17:18.055 --> 00:17:21.391
Since we're both orphans,
maybe we should adopt a child.

00:17:21.475 --> 00:17:24.311
Adoption? Yes, that's acceptable.

00:17:24.394 --> 00:17:28.649
Heck, it's more than acceptable,
it's adequately satisfactory.

00:17:33.278 --> 00:17:36.031
Hello? Imperial Dragon Restaurant?

00:17:36.114 --> 00:17:38.700
I've got a herd of you-know-what's
for sale.

00:17:39.409 --> 00:17:40.744
Let me check.

00:17:40.827 --> 00:17:43.580
Oh, aren't you a cutie?

00:17:43.664 --> 00:17:45.666
About 35 pounds.

00:17:46.833 --> 00:17:48.126
What?

00:17:49.711 --> 00:17:52.506
Hi, Bender. We'd like to adopt a child.

00:17:52.589 --> 00:17:54.675
Well, you've come to the right place.

00:17:54.758 --> 00:17:58.637
Because Honest Bender's Orphanarium
means discount orphans.

00:17:58.720 --> 00:18:02.891
Now, little lady, what do I have to do
to send you home with 12 orphans today?

00:18:02.975 --> 00:18:04.893
Uh, I'm afraid we only want one.

00:18:04.977 --> 00:18:07.771
Whatever you say, chief.
I'll show you what I got in stock.

00:18:07.854 --> 00:18:10.065
I remember this from when we were kids.

00:18:10.148 --> 00:18:12.818
The warden would trot you out
in front of prospective parents,

00:18:12.901 --> 00:18:14.820
and they'd judge you like a piece of meat.

00:18:14.903 --> 00:18:17.531
- I'm Albert.
- Kind of fatty.

00:18:17.614 --> 00:18:19.074
Then how 'bout this little number?

00:18:19.157 --> 00:18:21.576
Purebred human. No vampire in there.

00:18:21.994 --> 00:18:23.704
- Uh... Mmm...
- Well...

00:18:25.038 --> 00:18:26.331
If you're strapped for cash,

00:18:26.415 --> 00:18:28.792
you might want to consider
this irregular unit.

00:18:28.917 --> 00:18:32.212
Cursed with a third ear,
but so full of that emotion

00:18:32.296 --> 00:18:34.798
I understand is called "love."

00:18:34.881 --> 00:18:38.093
One time, I did a hundred jump ropes.

00:18:38.218 --> 00:18:41.888
Oh! I can't decide!
We're gonna have to think about it.

00:18:41.972 --> 00:18:44.850
Okay, kids. Grown-ups gotta talk now.
Time for bed.

00:18:44.933 --> 00:18:47.227
But it's 10:00 in the morning!

00:18:47.311 --> 00:18:48.979
I said, hit the hay!

00:18:54.359 --> 00:18:56.570
Oh, they're all so adorable.

00:18:56.653 --> 00:18:58.864
Yeah. You know,

00:18:58.947 --> 00:19:02.451
it's times like this,
I can hardly bear to let them go.

00:19:02.534 --> 00:19:05.329
Good night, you princes of Maine!

00:19:05.412 --> 00:19:07.831
You kings of New New England!

00:19:07.914 --> 00:19:09.958
You're under arrest for child cruelty,

00:19:10.042 --> 00:19:12.461
child endangerment,
depriving children of food,

00:19:12.544 --> 00:19:13.837
selling children as food

00:19:13.920 --> 00:19:15.756
and misrepresenting
the weight of livestock.

00:19:16.840 --> 00:19:19.676
If you had kids of your own,
you'd understand.

00:19:22.179 --> 00:19:25.390
Officer, would it be all right
if we adopted one of the kids?

00:19:25.474 --> 00:19:28.518
Might as well. They're just gonna
rot in the evidence locker.

00:19:29.978 --> 00:19:31.396
Nice ear!

00:19:32.522 --> 00:19:34.441
Hey, Three Ears!

00:19:36.109 --> 00:19:37.569
I've made up my mind.

00:19:37.653 --> 00:19:38.946
Let's adopt her.

00:19:39.029 --> 00:19:41.281
Her? But there's plenty of normal ones.

00:19:41.365 --> 00:19:44.534
Come on, Adlai.
She could really use a mom and dad.

00:19:44.618 --> 00:19:49.331
Ear Face! Ear Face!
Sally won the ugly race!

00:19:49.414 --> 00:19:51.792
On the other hand,
the children bring up a good point.

00:19:51.875 --> 00:19:54.878
- She does have an ear on her face.
- Well? So what?

00:19:54.962 --> 00:19:58.173
She may be different,
but she still deserves a good home.

00:19:58.256 --> 00:20:00.509
Oh, all right.
If you really want that one,

00:20:00.592 --> 00:20:03.095
I can give her an operation
to make her acceptable.

00:20:03.178 --> 00:20:07.099
She doesn't need an operation.
She's fine the way she is.

00:20:07.182 --> 00:20:09.559
Oh, and I suppose
you were fine the way you were?

00:20:09.643 --> 00:20:12.020
- Damn right I was!
- Yay!

00:20:12.104 --> 00:20:13.188
Shut up, Fry.

00:20:13.272 --> 00:20:16.066
Now, look, Adlai.
I'm proud to be different.

00:20:16.149 --> 00:20:19.194
And I just wish I'd realized
that when I was her age.

00:20:19.278 --> 00:20:21.530
I also have a tail!

00:20:21.613 --> 00:20:25.367
Now, take me to the hospital and put
my eye back the way it was. Right now!

00:20:25.450 --> 00:20:26.660
Why should I do that?

00:20:26.743 --> 00:20:27.911
Listen, buddy.

00:20:27.995 --> 00:20:31.331
By the end of the day,
one of us is gonna have one eye.

00:20:33.208 --> 00:20:36.003
In recognition of Bender's generous gift

00:20:36.086 --> 00:20:40.090
of 12 orphans and a government check
for 1,200 wing-wangs,

00:20:40.173 --> 00:20:43.093
I hereby rename this building

00:20:43.176 --> 00:20:46.346
the Bender B. Rodriguez Orphanarium.

00:20:50.851 --> 00:20:53.687
It's good to have
the old weird-looking Leela back.

00:20:53.812 --> 00:20:56.315
Oh, you're a true friend, Fry.

00:20:56.398 --> 00:20:58.984
I guess there's nothing wrong
with being a little weird.

00:20:59.067 --> 00:21:02.321
Leela, there's nothing
wrong with anything.

00:21:02.404 --> 00:21:04.072
We'll miss you, Daddy Bender.

00:21:04.156 --> 00:21:07.326
We know robots don't have emotions,

00:21:07.409 --> 00:21:09.620
but we drawed you this picture.

00:21:09.703 --> 00:21:13.457
So if you ever miss us,
even just a teeny bit,

00:21:13.540 --> 00:21:14.958
you can look at it.

00:21:15.042 --> 00:21:18.420
Hey, I smoke a cigar,
not a candy cane. Sheesh!

00:21:22.007 --> 00:21:23.342
Aw...

00:21:39.983 --> 00:21:41.735
Hey, what the... Whoa!

00:21:41.818 --> 00:21:43.779
Get away! Come on.

00:21:43.862 --> 00:21:46.073
I just got all the gum off of there.

00:21:46.156 --> 00:21:47.991
Hey! Hey!

00:21:48.055 --> 00:21:49.681
I hate you!

00:21:49.785 --> 00:21:51.912
I hate you all!